next a $0 audit of the shared fiscal-year note's consumers and effects | in force | `unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/AUDIT-RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:952:| D608 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 150): the fiscal-note lead closes as cleanup-only (no demonstrated product effect; the clause is not inert because check 5 refuses a pre-year-end day; the reader split's cause not established); a reflection council (fresh Codex, cold read) follows | in force | `unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/fiscal-note/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:953:| D609 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (reflection council, cold Codex read): the next production step is a $0 source-to-request trace of the company's own figures on the carried fortnight (D505), by member, with time, duplicate, population and relevance controls and an independent second reader on bearing cases; moves only on a shared, consequential delivery mechanism | in force | `reflection-5/codex-cold.md`, `reflection-5/codex-challenge-1.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:954:| D610 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (reflection council): the company-figure delivery route closes narrowly (5 bearing undelivered statements on 3 questions, two mechanisms, none predicted to move an answer by a blind second reader with working controls; 49 groups homeless by D382/D384); no v12 effect test; next a $0 feasibility review of a same-news product comparison from established libraries | in force | `delivery-trace/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:955:| D611 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439: the same-news comparison from established libraries closes (D517's power arithmetic unchanged by a starting library; the old library ends 08-28; no exposure-free week remains from 09-21 to 10-26); nothing run | in force | `comparison-feasibility/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:956:| D612 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 151): paid work held on the currently supported candidates (every bounded route closed with evidence; A2 cannot be decided on stored topics); the running system stays the default; reopen on new consequential delivery cases, decidable comparison material, Alex's marks or decisions, or a new concrete reversible candidate | in force | `reflection-4/council-codex-151.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:957:| D613 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 152): D611's exposure claim corrected (07-20..08-24 unread by any new-system Step 1 run); D612's hold stands; official gate 1 already meets lines 2 and 5 on the 44 and misses zero-fault lines 1, 3, 4 by 6 sends of 131 of different meanings; no code check or send on them | in force | `reflection-4/council-codex-152.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:958:| D614 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 153): the refusal census (174 over 30 topics; 13 unjustified on 6, all 'none main') maps to the closed main-part class; D612 stands; next a $0 design review of splitting (separate topics vs two judged questions under one topic) against D397, D436, D38 with the guards; no version opened, D397 unchanged | in force | `refusal-census/RESULT.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:959:| D615 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council round 154): the period split (D38's one view a year; the step names a typed 'one quantity for two periods' case, code splits by the years named) is developed at $0 as a lead on D397's open defect; no gate movement claimed; probe only after a reviewed design | in force | `splitting/DESIGN-REVIEW.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:960:| D616 | 2026-11-16 | Under D439 (council rounds 155 to 158): the period split's design v4 accepted for a $0 scratch build beside the frozen ladder step; the narrow D397 departure (one judged question per open year for one quantity over two open years) recorded as a reversible proposal, not in force; Stage B readers refuse split stores; nothing sent | in force | `splitting/DESIGN.md` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:987:| D643 | 2026-11-16 | Gate-1 launch prepared as an inert draft for Alex (`reflection-6/gate1-candidate/`): Stage A on the 44 × 3 with astra-frozen or astra-a2-v2, byte-checked,