{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10991,11009p;11867,11904p;11928,11956p'\"","aggregated_output":" 10991\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n 10992\t\n 10993\t- **The questions** (after D725):\n 10994\t  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n 10995\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n 10996\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n 10997\t  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n 10998\t    (recommended); 暂不定.\n 10999\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n 11000\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11001\t  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n 11002\t    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n 11003\t    ceiling.\n 11004\t  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n 11005\t    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n 11006\t- poc-v118 stays the product.\n 11007\t\n 11008\t## D727 · 2026-11-22 · judging-v13's $0 gate: the design passed council (round 46e); gate runs 1–6 and council rounds 46f–46j; the gate is not yet passed; one choice goes to Alex\n 11009\t\n 11867\t## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n 11868\t\n 11869\t- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\n 11870\t  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n 11871\t  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\n 11872\t- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\n 11873\t  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\n 11874\t     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\n 11875\t     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \"not started\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\n 11876\t  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\n 11877\t     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\n 11878\t     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\n 11879\t  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\n 11880\t     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n 11881\t  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n 11882\t     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\n 11883\t- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\n 11884\t\n 11885\t## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\n 11886\t\n 11887\t- **Under D439 and D758.** Release work was opened by council 73 (D758). This slice carries it out locally at $0. Nothing is\n 11888\t  committed, pushed, published or deployed. The POC is unchanged: no POC code imports the release module.\n 11889\t- **The design** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`):\n 11890\t  - revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten rounds (74 to 74j);\n 11891\t  - revision 11 records the build changes required by councils 75 to 75f.\n 11892\t\n 11893\t  It holds:\n 11894\t  - one allow-listed exporter: a number question carries its question, its evidence in force and \"Forecast unavailable\"; an event or\n 11895\t    Yes/No question carries its question, evidence and answer labels (D758 §4 a);\n 11896\t  - the writer refuses an off-list field;\n 11897\t  - the pass condition: every package field compared with its stored source at the bound, derived from the store;\n 11898\t  - a staged check before one atomic no-replace publication (`renamex_np` with `RENAME_EXCL`);\n 11899\t  - reports published by a no-replace link;\n 11900\t  - canonical days; keys counted only once visible at the bound; store paths free of URI syntax; package files read once.\n 11901\t- **Built:** `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n 11902\t- **Proof** (`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`):\n 11903\t  - 36 release tests;\n 11904\t  - full suite 425 passed;\n 11928\t  - commit, publish and deploy, which remain Alex's.\n 11929\t\n 11930\t## D760 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 2 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release (the reader's page) is built and accepted at $0, and D756's screen check passes (councils 76–76h design, 77–77b build); nothing committed or published\n 11931\t\n 11932\t- **Under D439, D758 and D759.** D758 ordered the exporter first and the reader's screen second. This slice completes D756's screen\n 11933\t  check, locally at $0. Nothing is committed, pushed, published or deployed. The POC is unchanged.\n 11934\t- **The design** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md`, revision 7) was ready per council 76h after eight\n 11935\t  rounds. It holds:\n 11936\t  - a separate page that is a pure function of the package data;\n 11937\t  - the data embedded with literal JSON escapes;\n 11938\t  - a strict CSP: only the template's own hashed script and style, no connection, image, font, base or form target;\n 11939\t  - no links: source addresses are plain text;\n 11940\t  - no idea input;\n 11941\t  - the package is format `hivemind-release/2`, adding `index.html` and `page_sha256`. `check_package` requires the page to equal\n 11942\t    `render_page` of the very data bytes it checked;\n 11943\t  - the whole template is pinned by its sha256 (test 29).\n 11944\t- **The screen check** (`release_screen.mjs`; run `poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/`; expectation frozen beforehand from the\n 11945\t  accepted slice-1 packages) passed in headless Chrome 158 through its DevTools protocol:\n 11946\t  - `old-1/v8` shows its question, \"Open\", \"Forecast unavailable\" and \"1284 pieces of evidence\". Expanded, all 1,284 groups equal the\n 11947\t    frozen page, the same after closing and reopening;\n 11948\t  - every normal visit makes one request, the page itself, with no error;\n 11949\t  - at 390 px there is no horizontal scroll and Morningstar's quote wraps on screen; dark and light are the literal page colours;\n 11950\t  - every read text passes the not-clipped and 4.5:1 contrast rules;\n 11951\t  - the dated `old-3/v36` (2026-08-25) and `old-1/v10` (2026-08-28) show \"Answer: Yes\" with their one entry and nothing else;\n 11952\t  - a hostile quote shows as text with no image;\n 11953\t  - the page renders in 0.05 s and is 5,794,595 bytes against 5,788,634 of data.\n 11954\t- **Eight negative pages were each caught for their own reason:**\n 11955\t  - a restored fetch, by a named `connect-src` violation;\n 11956\t  - an extra forecast line inside the card, and the same line beside it;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
