{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md | sed -n '478,511p'; rg -n -m 1 -o '.{0,250}more than double that next year.{0,85}' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-plan.json\"","aggregated_output":"   478\t   - switch reasons.\n   479\t\n   480\t   Search every decoded string field of the package for each, with no floor. List every hit with its question, field, evidence id\n   481\t   and the stored string it matched, and read each by hand. A genuine source quote, such as `e1865`'s \"Bullish\", is recorded as such.\n   482\t8. **Budgets:** bytes and seconds against the budgets above.\n   483\t\n   484\t## 8. A disclosed property, not built: evidence summaries keep extraction's wording\n   485\t\n   486\tThe release shows each evidence summary as extraction stored it; the release computes or converts nothing. A summary can make\n   487\tcontext explicit or restate a source figure by arithmetic, attributed to its source: `old-1/e3238` gives \"more than $40 billion in\n   488\tFY2028\" for a quote's \"more than double that next year\".\n   489\t- **Measured:** 25.6%, 25.2% and 25.4% of evidence in force in `old-1`, `old-2` and `old-3`, and 35.0% in the served ledger, carry a\n   490\t  number not in their quote. In a sample of 24, 23 are context: a year, a date, a quarter, a product name, an amount from the previous\n   491\t  sentence. One restates \"close to doubling\" as \"nearly 100%\".\n   492\t- **Why this is not the forecast D726 withholds.** Extraction never sees the system's forecast. Its request lists each open question\n   493\t  only as id, object, due day, question and a \"takes\" line (`placement.py:19-61`, `extraction.py:398-400`); no rung, label or\n   494\t  judged position.\n   495\t- **Council 74b** (`codex-r74b.md` §2) verified that extraction sends no rung, label or judged position, and that the census\n   496\t  reproduces.\n   497\t- **The disagreement that remains is narrow.**\n   498\t  - Codex reads revision 4's \"amounts as quoted\" as requiring source wording for a calculated amount attributed to a source, such\n   499\t    as `e3238`'s \"more than $40 billion\".\n   500\t  - Claude reads it as \"the release computes or converts nothing\".\n   501\t  - Both agree: no digit filter, no change to extraction.\n   502\t- **The course taken.** By AGENTS' rule for an unsettled disagreement, the cheaper, reversible course is to keep the stored summary.\n   503\t  The quote is shown beside it, so the source wording is on the reader's screen. A later version can drop the field from the\n   504\t  allow-list or change it.\n1:48df2272209cf74248fae 2026-08-28] NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2933, e3356,\n1:48df2272209cf74248fae 2026-08-28] NVIDIA projected stand-alone CPU revenue of $20 billion in FY2027 and more than $40 billion in FY2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia is leaning into that opening, projecting $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and more than double that next year\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2933, e3356,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
