{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'e3238|more than double that next year' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md | cut -c1-650\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'e3238|more than double that next year' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r74b.md | cut -c1-650\"","aggregated_output":"20:**I still disagree on “amounts as quoted.”** Keeping `e3238` does not disclose a D726 judgement. But I read the underlying article: it says `$20 billion` and “more than double that next year.” The stored summary says **NVIDIA projected more than $40 billion**. The arithmetic is faithful. The attributed dollar figure is extraction’s wording. Revision 4 explicitly requires “amounts as quoted,” so I would use the source wording for that amount. The disagreement is narrow and does not justify a digit filter or a change to extraction. Under the stated council fallback, keeping the stored summary is the cheaper reversible course, with this excep\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
