{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sqlite3 'file:poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite?immutable=1&mode=ro' '.schema evidence' | head -40\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4871,4878p;11914,11929p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/release.py | sed -n '517,525p'\"","aggregated_output":"CREATE TABLE evidence (evidence_id text primary key, quote text, one_line text, speaker text, original_who text, original_day text, tier text, event_time text, created_seq integer, created_from_input text);\nCREATE TRIGGER evidence_no_update before update on evidence begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end;\nCREATE TRIGGER evidence_no_delete before delete on evidence begin select raise(abort, 'append-only'); end;\n  4871\t## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n  4872\t\n  4873\t- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n  4874\t- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n  4875\t- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n  4876\t- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, \"Authority and scope\" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 \"Own the loop\"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\n  4877\t- **Scope:** all modules Alex has taken up; the current work is clean Step 1 (gates 2 and 3 of `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/COMBINED-PLAN.md`), then the Step 4 judgement faults that kept Stage B from passing.\n  4878\t\n 11914\t    - a closing reason naming the band is absent;\n 11915\t    - packages are 0.37–0.40 of the existing library's size, at 1.25–1.28 times its time.\n 11916\t  - The diagnostic search found no condition, reason, explanation, implied outcome, reference or closing reason anywhere. Its 32\n 11917\t    distinct label texts are all source wording, read by hand.\n 11918\t- **What the councils taught** (each in `codex-r74*.md`, `codex-r75*.md`):\n 11919\t  - a check that searches strings misses a forecast restated in other words; compare each field with its origin;\n 11920\t  - a checker must derive the date, the class and the record list from the store, never from the package;\n 11921\t  - one structural rule for every public write: nothing replaces an existing path;\n 11922\t  - one for verification: compare against fixed values written before the run, and match each refusal's exact reason.\n 11923\t- **Recorded disagreement** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8): evidence summaries are kept as extraction stored them, beside their quotes.\n 11924\t  Codex would use source wording for an attributed calculated amount. The cheaper, reversible course was taken.\n 11925\t- **Not done, and next:**\n 11926\t  - slice 2, the release page that reads only the package, with a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen (D756's screen check);\n 11927\t  - the idea path in the release, deferred by council 74;\n 11928\t  - commit, publish and deploy, which remain Alex's.\n 11929\t\n   517\t    \"var data=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('release-data').textContent);\"\n   518\t    \"var root=document.getElementById('release');\"\n   519\t    \"function el(tag,cls,text){var e=document.createElement(tag);if(cls){e.className=cls;}if(text!==undefined){e.textContent=text;}return e;}\"\n   520\t    \"function piece(e){var item=el('li','evidence-item');\"\n   521\t    \"item.appendChild(el('p','evidence-label','Hivemind summary'));item.appendChild(el('p','evidence-summary',e.one_line));\"\n   522\t    \"item.appendChild(el('p','evidence-label','Source quote'));\"\n   523\t    \"item.appendChild(el('blockquote','evidence-quote',e.quote));\"\n   524\t    \"item.appendChild(el('p','evidence-meta',e.tier+' \\\\u00b7 '+e.speaker+' \\\\u00b7 original: '+e.original_who+(e.original_day?', '+e.original_day:'')));\"\n   525\t    \"var sources=el('ul','source-list');\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
