{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: consensus on (b).** For `old-1/e3238`, the source says NVIDIA projected $20 billion in stand-alone CPU revenue this year and “more than double that next year.” Hivemind’s summary may say NVIDIA projected **more than $40 billion** next year. Both sentences describe the same projection and preserve the same lower bound. [RELEASE-BUILD.md:486](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md:486)\n\n1. **Conditions.** “Amounts as quoted” applies to the text labelled **Source quote**, which must reproduce the passage verbatim. The adjacent **Hivemind summary** may use a dollar amount that follows directly from that passage and preserves its qualifiers. Here, “more than” matters. An exact $40 billion would change the claim. [FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:49) · [codex-r78.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r78.md:3)\n2. **Authority.** D439 and D758 give the council authority to settle this local release choice. Alex’s D726 withholds Hivemind’s own forecast band, forecast text and history. The dollar figure here comes entirely from the source’s projection. The release displays the stored summary, so (b) requires no change to extraction. [DECISIONS-log.md:4874](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4874) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11869](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11869) · [DECISIONS-log.md:11004](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11004)\n3. **Disposition.** This resolves round 78’s open disagreement on attributed, calculated amounts. The decision is the council’s interpretation of the release design. This review made no file changes. [codex-r78.md:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r78.md:12)"}}
